# Creating Visualizations

## 📝 To Do
#### Practice building graphs in Google Sheets. Start by making a copy of the data so you can edit it:

#### 1. Open the <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1AlVNpxzypX82fNlPDxDEa5ww72J_G2kyfZ2sFJedBJA/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">School Party Survey Data - Google Sheets</a></p>
#### 2. Create a Copy of the dataset before creating a data visualization.

#### Now that you have the data, create at least one of the following charts. If you have time and want to explore, try creating both a bar chart and pie chart.

---

<img src="https://images.code.org/fc0d828145861e665d2b0f0eabfc1dc1-image-1744901010152.png" alt="bar chart created in Google Sheets" width="250px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 0 40px 40px;">

## Bar Chart
#### Using the pizza party data, create a bar chart by:
#### 1. Go to the "Bar Chart Workspace Tab"
#### 2. Highlight the column of data you want to use.
#### 3. Select 'insert' graph from the drop down menu.
#### 4. Select 'bar chart' from the side menu.

<details><summary style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>🔎 Show Me How 🔎</strong></summary> <img src="https://images.code.org/b6042703403f38487c31c55e8e9f238b-makechart.gif">
</details>

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

<img src="https://images.code.org/1614544f27bed480f32d75c583ac4b19-image-1744901246487.png" alt="pie chart created in Google Sheets" width="250px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 0 40px 40px;">

## Pie Chart

#### Using the pizza party data, create a bar chart by:
#### 1. Go to the "Pie Chart Workspace"
#### 2. Highlight the column of data you want to use.
#### 3. Select 'insert' graph from the drop down menu.
#### 4. Select 'pie chart' from the side menu.

<details><summary style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>🔎 Show Me How 🔎</strong></summary> <img src="https://images.code.org/b6042703403f38487c31c55e8e9f238b-makechart.gif">
</details>

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

